      "end": 1.75,
      "text": "Hey, how's your week going?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 8.73,
      "end": 16.46,
      "text": "Strain out the food bits first and pack them out with your trash. Then scatter the water widely, at least a couple hundred feet from any stream or lake."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 20.21,
      "end": 26.27,
      "text": "Yes, even then. Biodegradable soap still needs soil to break down, it's not safe straight into water."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 33.66,
      "end": 38.55,
      "text": "Better not. Animals dig them up and get used to people food. Pack them out with everything else."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.28,
      "end": 49.53,
      "text": "Ha, it is. A trick is to scrape the pot really well and use hot water, then you barely need soap at all."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 54.34,
      "end": 55.823,
      "text": "The wildlife thanks you."
    }
